# Calcium dynamics and bone remodeling

This repository contains a Julia-first model library and a public model atlas
for calcium–phosphate homeostasis and the bone-remodeling mechanisms that
directly couple to it.

**Live atlas:** https://azelys.github.io/calcium/

**Canonical source:** https://github.com/azelys/calcium

## Scope

The public literature map uses a strict inclusion rule. A model must either:

1. simulate calcium and/or phosphate dynamics directly; or
2. model a PTH-driven bone-resorption mechanism that is a direct component of
   the integrated calcium-homeostasis lineage.

This excludes general models of genetics, menopause, BMD-only trajectories,
fatigue, mechanics, and spatial remodeling when they do not represent mineral
fluxes or calcium-regulating endocrine physiology.

## Contents

- `julia/` — the only model implementation layer. It contains Julia
  translations of Kroll, Lemaire, Raposo, Peterson/Riggs–Khurana, and Granjon.
- `docs/index.html` — the static GitHub Pages atlas. It is a presentation
  artifact, not a second model implementation.
- `LITERATURE_REVIEW.md` — inclusion criteria, source audit, and the model
  replication plan.

Legacy non-Julia model sources have been intentionally removed. Local PDFs and
desktop/editor artifacts remain excluded by `.gitignore`.

## Run the Julia tests

```sh
julia --project=julia -e 'using Pkg; Pkg.test()'
```

